[{"id":2575419274,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6ZgceK","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","login":"ryevdokimov","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov"},"body":"This will crash if [physics runs on a separate thread](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_projectsettings.html#class-projectsettings-property-physics-3d-run-on-separate-thread), check `NOTIFICATION_PHYSICS_PROCESS` in `Node3DEditorViewport` to see how this was handled for similar functionality. ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#pullrequestreview-2575419274","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102085","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-01-27T13:19:59Z"},{"id":2607381750,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6baXz2","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1045636?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/geowarin","id":1045636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDU2MzY=","login":"geowarin","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/geowarin"},"body":"It works great! Nice QOL feature.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/49cb631e-5e2b-430c-a201-822495876048)\r\n\r\nThanks @GustJc for this PR and for its accompanying Youtube video (Create a NEW feature to Godot (C++) | How to contribute code), showing people the process of contributing to the engine.\r\n\r\nHandling threaded physics adds a little bit of complexity and duplication but it seems reasonable.\r\n\r\nIn the future, I think it would be nice if \"snap to colliders\" also worked when dragging an existing point. Maybe in another PR?\r\n","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#pullrequestreview-2607381750","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102085","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-02-10T23:11:24Z"},{"id":3703119683,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7cuR9D","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","login":"ryevdokimov","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov"},"body":"If `Snap to Colliders` is checked, and you try to add a point to empty space, nothing happens which is confusing. It should fall back to plane intersection, which is how similar functionality handles it (collision repositioning or instantiating). ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#pullrequestreview-3703119683","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102085","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-01-25T03:06:26Z"},{"id":3746914267,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7fVV_b","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","login":"ryevdokimov","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"u